#except
-----
this except let us handle the errors in the code
syntax--except:

try:
    num=int(input("Enter a num:"))
except NameError:
    print('will get name error')

try:
    num=int(input("Enter a num:"))
except ValueError:
    print('will get name error')
    
try:
    num=int(input("Enter a num:"))
    num_2=int(input("Enter a num:"))
    print(num/num_2)
except:
    print('will get name error')

#else
-----
if the try block does not have any error than the else block will execute
eg:-
try:
    num = int(input("Enter a num:"))
    num_2= int(input("Enter a  num:"))
    print(num/num_2)
except ZeroDivisionError:
    print('will get zerodivison Error')
except ValueError:
    print('will get name error')
else:
    print('no error')
 
#finally
--------
the finally block will excute either code contain error or not
eg:-

try:
    num = int(input("Enter a num:"))
    num_2= int(input("Enter a  num:"))
    print(num/num_2)
except ZeroDivisionError:
    print('will get zerodivison Error')
except ValueError:
    print('will get name error')
else:
    print('no error')
finally:
    print('end')
  

